    "narrative": "Our lineup for August 15th features high-upside plays anchored by favorable matchups against sub-par arms. **Brendan Donovan** (68.26) and **Gleyber Torres** (67.45) stand as our strongest starts; **Brendan Donovan** leverages a massive 14% platoon boost against Hayden Wesneski, while **Gleyber Torres** benefits from a rare combination of leadoff duties and a strong platoon edge against Anthony Kay. **Jung Hoo Lee** (67.22) and **Zack Gelof** (58.70) are also prioritized for their speed potential, as both get a boost from facing pitchers with slow deliveries, creating ideal scenarios to hunt for the stolen bases that remain our primary objective for the week. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (68.48) continues to be an essential anchor despite the lack of a specific opposing pitcher data point today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **JJ Bleday** (48.77), who narrowly missed the cut. While he possesses a decent baseline, his score was suppressed by a poor platoon dynamic against Ryan Gusto and a 40% rain risk, which ultimately made him a liability compared to the higher floor provided by our current outfield depth. **Yainer Diaz** (45.40) is our most marginal start, and he remains active only because the positional requirements allow it; he faces the highest risk today, as his batting order position (#9) significantly handicaps his counting stat ceiling against Emerson Hancock. All managers should monitor the official lineups closely, as our projections currently rely on assumed batting orders which, if shifted, could necessitate a late-bench swap.",
